    <item>
      <title>Evaluate agent-team fit separately from solo capability</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/agent-patterns/multi-agent.html#november-2026-a-solo-winner-may-be-a-poor-teammate</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-23:agent-team-fit</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:47:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Added qualified optimisation-benchmark evidence and corrected blanket coordination advice. Updated Week 4 card 14, protected performance checks and bootstrap guidance. Compare team fit, resource cost and integration effort before scaling agents. Source: https://frontier.replit.com/throwing-headcount-at-the-problem/ . Vendor results are not a general productivity guarantee.</description>
      <category>Agent coordination</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>YouTube topic sections and a dedicated video RSS feed</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/videos/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-23:youtube-collection</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 07:19:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Added a shared collection of 19 YouTube talks, interviews and demos covering context engineering, agents, spec workflows and verification. Every guide topic and engineer/company profile now has a video subsection, with explicit gaps where no suitable selection exists. The daily research refresh now searches for relevant additions. Subscribe to the separate video feed at https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/videos.xml .</description>
      <category>Learning resources</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Separate knowledge-gap reports from shared rules</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/context-engineering/knowledge-layer.html#november-2026-report-gaps-before-promoting-shared-knowledge</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-22:knowledge-curation-proposals</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:49:24 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Added a knowledge-curation pattern: report missing or wrong guidance separately, then verify source and scope before promoting a correction into shared instructions. The guide, learning card and two bootstrap adaptations now make this distinction explicit. Source: https://www.langchain.com/blog/knowledge-factory . This is a coding adaptation of a practitioner account, not a demonstrated productivity gain.</description>
      <category>Context engineering</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Keep specs maintained and tool access enforced</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/study-briefings/2026-11-20.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-20:spec-maintenance-tool-policy</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:54:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Qualified blanket spec and fixed tool-count recommendations using an SDD field study and primary tool-policy documentation. Added spec-maintenance ownership and checks that distinguish discovery from enforced access, with matching learning-card and bootstrap updates. Sources: https://arxiv.org/html/2608.25202v5 ; https://docs.langchain.com/langsmith/tool-gateway-policies ; https://www.langchain.com/blog/langsmith-tool-gateway .</description>
      <category>Research corrections</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Measure repeatability and task-specific outcomes</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/study-briefings/2026-11-19.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-19:repeatability-context-evidence</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:23:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Added a dated Pocock feature account, Datadog security-hunt repeatability evidence and task-specific evaluation guidance from OpenAI. These help separate reported practice, repeatable checks and activity metrics. Updated profiles, slides, comparison notes, the atlas and bootstrap adaptations. Sources: https://www.aihero.dev/watch-me-ship-a-21-000-line-feature-with-mattpocock-skills~ez95n ; https://www.datadoghq.com/blog/datadogs-agentic-vulnerability-hunting-system/ ; https://openai.com/index/research-acceleration-jagged-frontier/ .</description>
      <category>Research updates</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Check every tool path; ground memory and CI repair in evidence</title>
      <link>https://bnppl.github.io/good-vibes/study-briefings/2026-11-18.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">good-vibes:2026-11-18:containment-memory-ci</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 08:53:15 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Added tool-path containment checks, qualified memory-consolidation evidence and reviewable acceptance data; refreshed Willison safeguards and PostHog CI repair evidence, slides, atlas and bootstrap recipes. These distinguish prototypes and team reports from proven general benefits. Sources: https://blog.primeradiant.com/external-sandboxes-for-coding-agents/ ; https://posthog.com/blog/self-driving-ci ; https://www.anthropic.com/research/components-of-agent-memory ; https://www.martinfowler.com/articles/tests-as-data.html .</description>
      <category>Research updates</category>
    </item>
